cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ShortSeq in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "ShortSeq: A benchmark for foundation model evaluation on short time series"
abstract: >-
  ShortSeq evaluates classical, machine-learning, and foundation-model
  forecasters on short time series, where the sample sizes that favour
  large pretrained models are absent. It provides a pip-installable
  package, a rolling one-step-ahead evaluation protocol with no
  look-ahead, and statistical significance testing (Diebold-Mariano with
  Bonferroni correction; Friedman omnibus with Nemenyi post-hoc).

  The benchmark comprises 368 series, split into a short stratum
  (n < 200, 199 series) and a long stratum (n >= 200, 169 series) that
  are analysed separately and never pooled. Of these, 366 are real series
  drawn from at most eight distinct upstream providers, and 2 are seeded
  simulations included for continuity with an earlier study. Note that
  the ten dataset keys in the registry are NOT ten independent sources:
  two are simulated, two cover a single M-competition, and one Kaggle
  release is held as two non-independent views.

  ShortSeq contributes dataset loaders, evaluation code, and computed
  results. It also distributes derived (aggregated or column-selected)
  series for several sources. The upstream terms of use for those sources
  are NOT yet recorded or verified, and several originate in Kaggle
  competition releases whose rules may restrict redistribution. See
  DATASHEET.md section 6.2 for the per-source status; treat the derived
  data as of uncertain licensing status until that table is completed.

  DATASHEET.md documents composition, provenance, preprocessing, known
  defects, and intended and discouraged uses in full.
